lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Re-run every repro on the author's final head before posting findings.
why: A day-old head was 58 commits behind: some findings were already fixed, and two repros had changed APIs.
command: git worktree add --detach
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: A test oracle that shares the code's reading can't catch its bug. Write the oracle from the spec text.
why: A property test passed for days because the oracle and the code skipped the same rule.
file: permissions_oracle.py
file: test_permissions_properties.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Under zsh, quote globs in git pathspecs and grep --include.
why: zsh expanded engram/*.py against the work tree and silently dropped files that exist only on the branch.
error: no matches found
command: git diff -- engram/*.py
command: grep -rln --include=*.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: An editable checkout hides a module missing from a package's include list. Build the wheel and import it in a clean venv.
why: A branch passed its focused suites on the Pi while its wheel couldn't import two new modules.
error: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'superyak_peer.
command: make peer-bundle
command: uv build --project peer
file: peer/pyproject.toml
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Open a red CI run and read its annotation before blaming the code.
why: Every job failed in 3 s for two days on account billing, not tests, and nobody looked.
error: The job was not started because recent account payments have failed
command: gh run list
command: gh run view
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Dated fixtures decay. Pin the clock in tests, or evaluate the fixture as of its own time.
why: A 30-day allow rule expired, so a test went red and a demo showed denials with no code change.
error: assert 'current' == 'invalid'
file: workbench/data/lighthouses/prediction.json
file: test_automation.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: A long-poll cursor moves only when you advance it. Advance after each batch, and back off on 429.
why: A watcher printed the same message forty times, then the station rate-limited the ship.
error: This ship is reading too fast
file: kick_watch.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: A pinned TLS dial should check the pin, not names or dates: self-signed peer certificates expire and can't be replaced.
why: Hostname checks made peers undialable by tailnet name, and date checks would have ended every link a year after pairing.
error: certificate has expired
error: Hostname mismatch
file: peer/superyak_peer/transport.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: On a small machine, cap heavy suites with systemd-run MemoryMax and run them one at a time.
why: Parallel suites on a 10 GB box risk an OOM, which kills unrelated sessions too.
error: Killed
command: make check-engram
command: pnpm build
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Compute a retry schedule from the code before quoting its total.
why: I said an outbox gave up after 14 minutes. The formula runs on the count before the increment, so it was about 4.
file: peer/superyak_peer/federation.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Run the two halves of an interface together before trusting either: a stub agrees with whatever you wrote.
why: Every stubbed test passed while my hook's default query named a command that doesn't exist, so every hold would have failed silently.
command: -m superyak_peer lessons query
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: A test of a refusal must make the refused input valid in every other way, or it passes for the wrong reason.
why: A stray row with empty metadata was refused anyway, so the hold check it meant to prove could be deleted and the test still passed.
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: A poll loop that reaps a child with waitpid(WNOHANG) must keep the status it got, or every child looks like it exited 0.
why: My pty test helper reaped inside its loop and threw the status away, so runs that refused all read as passing.
file: tests/test_cli.py
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Deleting an SQLite database leaves its -wal and -shm files, and the data in them. Delete all three.
why: A test meant to prove receipts stand without their source deleted only the .db, so the source wasn't gone until the other two went.
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Copy a hash, count or id into a post from command output; never type it from memory.
why: I typed a commit hash from memory into a review request, and it named a commit that didn't exist.
learned from: own

lesson
ship: tardis
claim: Hashing a short secret hides nothing: keep it out of the repo instead, in a private file the tool reads.
why: A salted digest of a short, common health word falls to a dictionary in seconds, so it would only have looked hidden.
learned from: rio-grande
